if you're an odesk contractor and you're  trying to win more jobs  i'm going to share with you the five  ways to wow  employers on odesk and land that job  hi i'm evan carmichael i believe in  entrepreneurs and i got a great question  from one of my youtube subscribers  albert  love you guys who wrote in to say hi  evan i'm about to start on odesk and  first i want to get all things ready i'm  a graphic designer and illustrator my  question is do employers get interested  on beginners  i mean i'm not a beginner but obviously  i would not have any feedback yet  because i'm starting it would be enough  with the skills and the tests to get  hired  albert albert fantastic question i'm a  huge supporter of odesk i've been an  employer there for a while  and i wanted to share with you my five  tips  for how you can stand out and wow  employers number one is write a great  bio what i look for in a bio it's not  just the skills you have but i want to  feel the passion for what you do  i want to know why you're doing what you  do and what excites you about it  so yes tell me your skills tell me where  you've worked tell me how many years  experience you have  but also tell me what makes you come  alive and why you do what you do  also make sure you get your bio checked  out by native english speakers so you  don't have errors in it  in your question to me you had a few  grammatical errors that  people don't care so much if you're a  graphic designer they're not hiring you  for your english skills  but every chance you have to impress a  client you want to take it so just get a  friend of yours who speaks english  fluently  to check out that bio and make sure  there are no mistakes  number two show you care about the  company one of the biggest pet peeves i  have with people who are applying for a  job for me on odesk or otherwise  is they do zero research into me and my  business  they just submit the form submit their  cover letter and fire it away  sometimes not even changing the name and  it's just saying dear sir or madam  if you want to stand out and really wow  the employer then do a little research  and digging into the business  visit my website and tell me what you  like about it follow me on social media  and respond to something that i've  posted  tell me what you really love about my  business and what attracts you to  working with me  i'd say only one percent of the people  who apply to a job  actually go that extra mile and i always  pay attention to those guys over  everybody else  number three is have a great picture  have a professional  full color picture of yourself that i  can clearly see your face and i can  relate to you  don't make your picture black and white  don't have a picture of you on the beach  don't have a picture of you in your  undershirt in your pajamas it's  professional you're trying to get a job  make it professional another thing i'd  say is make sure to smile in your  picture  i know a lot of people from different  cultures having a serious picture  serious face is is normal and standard  but if you want to work with north  americans we're used to seeing  smiling pictures for north american  employers  seeing somebody who's smiling makes us  relate to that person more makes us  like that person more and makes you more  likely to get a response from us  so have a great picture number four is  take the tests  so odess provides you all kinds of  different tasks that you can take to  showcase how great you are at different  software tools  this is especially important if you  don't have any work experience yet and  you're just getting started  you want to take those tests and it's  not just taking the test  it's doing well on the tests don't just  go into it saying yeah i know photoshop  will do that really well no problem  you need to score well you want to be in  the top 10 percent  of everybody on odesk was taking that  test so prepare for it  study for it and ace it because that  will really help make you stand out  versus everybody else on odesk and  number five is upload your portfolio  again this is super important if you  have zero work experience you want to be  able to show people that you have a  great portfolio and you know what you're  doing  i try to show a diverse range of  portfolio items  so that people know you can do a lot of  different things and as a bonus  if you really want to connect to the  north american employers  i try to have some north american  content in my portfolio  even if you've never actually worked  with a north american company before  just take a company and make a brochure  for them  because again as an employer if i'm  seeing something that i can relate to  that's in my language that is around the  company that i can understand  i'm much more likely to want to hire you  than if everything you have is in  another language on businesses that i  don't understand  so upload your portfolio and if you  don't have anything for a north american  company yet  create something so those are my five  tips write a great bio  show you care about the company have a  great picture  take the tests and upload your portfolio  and of course believe for those of you  watching i'd love for you to answer this  question  if you were considering hiring somebody  on odesk  and they had zero work experience that  they could share  there's their first contract what would  you look for what would you want to see  in somebody's response to you to get  them to wow you and make that memorable  leave that in the comments below i'd  love to hear what's on your mind and i  think others would really benefit from  it as well if you guys like this video  don't forget to subscribe to the channel  and to the newsletter  thank you so much for watching and i'll  see you soon
 

